Neoism
======

Neoism is a terminal-first workspace for code, notes, agents, and multiplayer
editing. The great majority of Neoism — its editor, agent runtime, workspace
daemon, sync/CRDT layer, notebooks, drawing surfaces, extensions system, and UI
chrome — is original work by the Neoism contributors, licensed under the MIT
License (see LICENSE).

This branch uses GPUIX for its frontend and Ghostty for terminal emulation.
GPUIX native and Solid bindings are distributed under Apache-2.0; their licenses
are included in desktop bundles as licenses/GPUIX-native.txt and licenses/GPUIX-solid.txt.
The retained CPU font/paint code, PTY support and configuration code include
Rio Terminal lineage. Upstream copyright and license notices remain applicable
where code is retained; source-file headers are authoritative.

